## Security Checklist

- [ ] No hardcoded secrets (use `vault_*` prefix for all secrets)
- [ ] Vault files properly encrypted
- [ ] `.vault_pass.txt` not in version control
- [ ] SSH key permissions are 0600
- [ ] Firewall rules are restrictive
- [ ] File permissions follow least privilege
- [ ] Jinja2 templates escape user input
- [ ] Services run with minimal privileges
- [ ] Docker containers run as non-root
- [ ] No sensitive data in logs

## AuroraOps-Specific Checks

- Verify all `vault_*` variables are properly defined in `secrets/vault.yml`
- Check that `certbot` credentials use vault references
- Ensure `singbox` UUIDs and keys come from vault
- Verify Bitwarden session files are not committed
- Check that `nodejs_opencode_server_password` uses vault reference

**Remember**: Security is not optional for infrastructure management. One leaked vault password can compromise all managed servers. Be thorough, be paranoid, be proactive.
